 "title": "haber ido, -ado / -ido as adjectives with estar, cansarse, es una silla mojada",
 "cards": [
  {
   "title": "After any form of haber, even 'to have'",
   "body": "",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I'll have lost it.",
     "es": "Lo habré perdido."
    },
    {
     "en": "I'd like to have gone.",
     "es": "Me gustaría haber ido."
    }
   ],
   "t": 0
  },
  {
   "title": "-ado / -ido as adjectives",
   "body": "Like English (sold, lost), the haber form also works as an adjective, which gives you hundreds of adjectives. After haber it never changes; as an adjective it agrees. These adjectives almost always go with estar.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I've closed it (the door).",
     "es": "La he cerrado."
    },
    {
     "en": "It's closed (the door).",
     "es": "Está cerrada."
    },
    {
     "en": "I'm lost.",
     "es": "Estoy perdido. / Estoy perdida."
    },
    {
     "en": "It's finished (the film).",
     "es": "Está terminada."
    },
    {
     "en": "They're sold (the houses).",
     "es": "Están vendidas."
    }
   ],
   "t": 60.7
  },
  {
   "title": "cansado comes from cansar",
   "body": "Cansar = to tire. Me canso = I get tired / fed up. Me he cansado = I've had enough.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I get tired.",
     "es": "Me canso."
    },
    {
     "en": "I've got tired.",
     "es": "Me he cansado."
    }
   ],
   "t": 276.0
  },
  {
   "title": "está cerrado vs es una persona cerrada",
   "body": "Idea is feminine. 'Es cerrado' sounds wrong; with persona, ser is fine.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "He's closed to the idea.",
     "es": "Está cerrado a la idea."
    },
    {
     "en": "He's a closed person.",
     "es": "Es una persona cerrada."
    }
   ],
   "t": 370.8
  },
  {
   "title": "Naming something always takes ser",
   "body": "'It's a chair' is about as characteristic as it gets, so ser, even with a state adjective added. Describing the chair's state on its own takes estar. Mojar = to wet.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "The chair is wet.",
     "es": "La silla está mojada."
    },
    {
     "en": "It's a wet chair.",
     "es": "Es una silla mojada."
    },
    {
     "en": "She's a lost person.",
     "es": "Es una persona perdida."
    }
   ],
   "t": 466.2
  }
 ],
